spaCy en_core_web_sm tokenizer, tagger weights and ports
========================================================

tokenizer.json holds the tokenizer settings of the spaCy pipeline
en_core_web_sm 3.8.0, extracted by build_tokenizer.py from spaCy 3.8:

  - the prefix, suffix, infix and URL patterns, rewritten from Python `re`
    syntax into `regexr` syntax with the same matches;
  - the tokenizer exceptions (special cases), unchanged;
  - spacy.lang.norm_exceptions.BASE_NORMS, unchanged;
  - the pipeline's `lexeme_norm` lookups table, unchanged, keyed by spaCy's
    string hash as the pipeline stores it.

src/g2p/spacy_tokenizer/ in this crate is a Rust port of spaCy 3.8's
spacy/tokenizer.pyx (Tokenizer.__call__ and the special-case matcher pass)
and of the English lexeme attribute getters in spacy/lang/lex_attrs.py. The
port changes the language and the data encoding. It keeps the behavior.

tagger.safetensors.zlib holds the trained parameters of the `tok2vec` and
`tagger` components of en_core_web_sm 3.8.0, unchanged in value, written by
convert_tagger.py as a zlib-compressed SafeTensors file. tagger.json holds
the network geometry, the HashEmbed seeds, the tag labels and the
spacy.symbols.IDS table, from the same pipeline and spaCy 3.8.

src/model/text/spacy_tagger/ in boostr is a Rust port of the forward pass
of spaCy 3.8's spacy.Tok2Vec.v2, MultiHashEmbed.v2, MaxoutWindowEncoder.v2
and spacy.Tagger.v2, and of the thinc 8.3 layers they build on (HashEmbed
with MurmurHash3_x86_128_uint64, Maxout, LayerNorm, expand_window/seq2col,
residual, with_array padding, Softmax_v2). src/g2p/spacy_tagger/ in this
crate ports spaCy's FeatureExtractor and StringStore ID lookup, and
src/g2p/misaki/preprocess.rs ports spaCy's Alignment.from_strings. The
ports change the language. They keep the behavior.

